## Errors & Mistakes
TestCompletion failed once after adding the subcommand: the "completion without a root" assertion expected output starting with ":" but got "repos\tList every repository that has plans\n:4\n". Cobra offers subcommand names whether or not the root resolves, which is correct, so the assertion now strips that one line and checks the directive follows. Also, an early shell command used echo ===== as a separator and zsh treated ===== as an =cmd expansion ("==== not found"); quote separators in zsh.

