## Hints for Future Agents
- get has both RunE with cobra.ArbitraryArgs and a subcommand. Cobra runs the subcommand when the first argument matches its name and otherwise falls through to RunE, so a plan whose short name is literally "repos" must be addressed by basename or path.
- The get -h Usage now shows two lines: "planner get [<plan>...] [flags]" and "planner get [command]".
- --repo is a substring match, so the labels get repos prints are candidates, not the only accepted values.
- Loose plans directly under the root have repo "" and are left out of get repos, as they were from completion.
- configs/herdr/config.toml was modified before this session and is intentionally not committed.

## Codebase Discoveries
- completeValues(values) is a reusable prefix filter; any fixed list completion should go through it rather than a hand-written loop.
- TestListGolden copies testdata/plans and testdata/external under a temp HOME and replaces the root with <root> in the output, so a golden for a command that prints only labels needs no path scrubbing.
- Cobra adds subcommand names to completions only when there are no positional args yet and no local non-persistent flag has been set; --root is persistent so it does not suppress them.

